James sought assistance in Julia to extract a ratio of `total_damage_countries` to `gdp` for specific years (2050) from two data frames within a dictionary. I provided a step-by-step guide that included filtering, joining the data frames, calculating the ratio, and grouping the results to compute summary statistics (mean, median, IQR). After encountering an error due to an undefined function `combinedata`, I corrected it to use the `combine` function. The revised code effectively computed the desired statistics for each country based on the calculated ratios while handling missing values properly.
